// Fast, seeded and cryptographic sources of randomness.
//
// > Randomness as a value, so a test can pin it down.
//
// A `Source` is a value carrying four functions, and every function here takes one as its first argument. Which source you pass decides where the bits come from; the code using it does not change.
//
// The three constructors differ only in that: `fast()` is seeded from the clock, `seeded(n)` produces the same sequence every run, and `strong()` uses the operating system's cryptographic generator.
//
// `HasFastRandom` and `HasStrongRandom` are separate attributes so that code needing secrecy has to say so, and cannot be handed a seeded generator by mistake.
mod code.knabel.dev.zirric_lang.zirric.random
